WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.002
Let's start off by talking about

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.253
work and studies.

00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:06.673
Currently I just graduated,

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.341
so I'm in between things.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.634
But yeah,

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.553
I am finding work at this point.

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:14.806
Ideally in Mumbai.

00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:16.808
I'm really interested

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:18.560
in like, the startup industry,

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.561
there are some startups

00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:21.563
that I'm looking to work with as of—

00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:23.314
in the moment, right now.

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:24.941
So that's just what, like,

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:26.735
this next chapter holds for me.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.948
Good question.

00:00:31.948 --> 00:00:34.325
I really feel strongly about philanthropy

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:36.578
and education specifically,

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.998
so I imagine myself living in between,

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:43.293
like, different places in India.

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:44.961
Pursuing this,

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:46.713
like, philanthropic

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:49.132
educational

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:51.259
work, yeah.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.305
So many things.

00:00:55.305 --> 00:00:56.848
You know, it's kind of like,

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:58.600
I don't know, I couldn't choose.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.726
I think every day

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.603
was something different.

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:04.397
I would watch, like, a really fun TV show

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.982
and, for example, Suits

00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:06.483
and be like,

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:07.692
“Oh, I'm going to be a lawyer.”

00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:08.985
And I was convinced.

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:10.737
And then I would watch a really fun movie

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.114
like Devil Wears Prada and...

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:14.991
I wanted to be a fashion designer.

00:01:14.991 --> 00:01:17.744
So it was many different things

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:18.912
when I was younger.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.497
Now let's talk about reading.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:23.917
So I don't know

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.960
if it’s necessarily my favorite,

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.629
but there is this book

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.631
called The Secret Garden

00:01:29.631 --> 00:01:32.050
that I remember reading in my class

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.510
in the fourth grade,

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.553
and I'm categorizing it

00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:36.930
as my favorite book

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.140
because it just meant a lot to me,

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.434
because there were really nice descriptions

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.186
about like, the scenery,

00:01:43.186 --> 00:01:46.064
and that really got me into reading.

00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:49.776
So I think for the heartwarming purpose,

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.820
it's definitely my favorite book

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.029
when I was younger,

00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:53.947
but it's just the book

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:54.948
that started my love

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.241
for reading in general.

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:00.245
I did a lot of reading.

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:01.121
Too much reading.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:03.206
I did a lot of reading

00:02:03.206 --> 00:02:05.583
that was more literary works

00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:06.751
and it made me realize,

00:02:06.751 --> 00:02:08.002
“Oh, I don't like it.”

00:02:08.002 --> 00:02:10.088
I don't like them.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:11.798
I'm also not a fan of novels,

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:14.050
but what I am a fan of is

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.011
more fiction or self-help

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:18.138
kind of books,

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.472
especially that I'm getting older

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.557
and I want to incorporate

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:22.058
habits into my life.

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:26.229
There's this book I read

00:02:26.229 --> 00:02:28.314
called Daisy Jones &amp; the Six

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.858
and it was just a really fun book.

00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:30.692
It was the book

00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:32.277
I read recently,

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:34.779
and I think people who are into fiction

00:02:34.779 --> 00:02:36.114
and like, music,

00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:37.782
would really love that book.

00:02:37.782 --> 00:02:40.368
It was adapted into a series after,

00:02:40.368 --> 00:02:42.829
so definitely recommend that one.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.539
Now let's talk about drinks

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.212
Okay, there's so many options.

00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:52.797
Particularly in my family,

00:02:52.797 --> 00:02:54.883
we have a weird mix of things,

00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:57.385
but in my country we usually have, like,

00:02:57.385 --> 00:02:58.887
masala chai,

00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:00.805
or we have normal sodas,

00:03:00.805 --> 00:03:02.515
but we put some masala in it,

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.892
which is like some spice

00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:06.394
to kind of give it that extra like kick.

00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:07.854
So that's really common.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:08.813
But in my family

00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:11.191
we put like, for example, Coke,

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.693
we put a little bit of vanilla ice cream.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.904
And I think it also has to do with

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:17.447
like, different places in India

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:18.656
also have this.

00:03:18.656 --> 00:03:20.950
But in my family it's staple.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:21.618
Yeah.

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:24.495
Yes, I do.

00:03:24.495 --> 00:03:26.039
And it's because

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.832
when I don’t, I can feel the

00:03:27.832 --> 00:03:29.626
like, adverse effects immediately.

00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:31.044
So I make sure

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.462
I drink water every single day.

00:03:32.462 --> 00:03:34.839
But it's so hard because

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:36.424
like, in the hurry of everything,

00:03:36.424 --> 00:03:37.175
you just forget.

00:03:39.302 --> 00:03:42.347
Okay, so I have phases in my life.

00:03:42.347 --> 00:03:44.432
Like, sometimes coffee

00:03:44.432 --> 00:03:45.642
just tastes too good,

00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:47.769
but I'm really caffeine sensitive.

00:03:47.769 --> 00:03:48.561
I've realized this

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.064
after having very, like,

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.649
jittery episodes,

00:03:52.649 --> 00:03:55.902
so if I have coffee, it's a decaf.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.153
But I really love tea

00:03:57.153 --> 00:03:58.488
for, like, different purposes.

00:03:58.488 --> 00:04:01.032
So like, camomile before sleeping

00:04:01.032 --> 00:04:02.408
or green tea to detox.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:08.915
Definitely tea.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.291
I think it's also like, culturally,

00:04:10.291 --> 00:04:11.376
like, we are more

00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:13.169
accustomed to being like,

00:04:13.169 --> 00:04:14.170
“Can I get you some tea?”

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.838
So, definitely tea.

00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:16.589
But also like,

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:19.259
coffee is always available if you want.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.718
But it’s a special request.

00:04:20.718 --> 00:04:22.262
Now let's talk about the weekend.

00:04:23.972 --> 00:04:27.225
So I think it depends on how the week has gone.

00:04:27.225 --> 00:04:28.601
If it’s a good week,

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.603
you know, weekend can go any which way.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.562
But I think

00:04:31.562 --> 00:04:33.231
a very crucial point,

00:04:33.231 --> 00:04:35.275
or part of my routine

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:37.944
is like, cold plunging or sauna.

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:40.488
I really try and prioritize that

00:04:40.488 --> 00:04:42.448
because it helps like,

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.493
my anxiety fade away.

00:04:45.493 --> 00:04:46.995
I really love exercising,

00:04:46.995 --> 00:04:50.123
that's a crucial part as well.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.916
And just meeting friends and family,

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:54.210
I think I carve out time

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.296
specifically for that because

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.089
the weekdays can get so busy.

00:05:00.383 --> 00:05:01.426
Very often.

00:05:01.426 --> 00:05:03.469
Like, most mornings are

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.263
like, they begin very lazily.

00:05:05.263 --> 00:05:07.056
And when it comes to lazy weekends,

00:05:07.056 --> 00:05:09.726
I don't really thrive on lazy weekends

00:05:09.726 --> 00:05:11.644
because then I kind of fall into like,

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:12.603
a rut.

00:05:12.603 --> 00:05:14.647
So I try to be lazy enough

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:15.690
but not too lazy.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.945
I definitely think so.

00:05:20.945 --> 00:05:22.447
I think that the more

00:05:22.447 --> 00:05:25.575
I'm using a lot of energy during the week,

00:05:25.575 --> 00:05:26.951
and maybe doing tasks

00:05:26.951 --> 00:05:27.994
that don't give me energy

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.245
that are more draining,

00:05:29.245 --> 00:05:30.872
I will need time to recuperate,

00:05:30.872 --> 00:05:32.707
like, during the weekends.

00:05:32.707 --> 00:05:34.584
So, the more

00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:37.128
I’m a little bit forced to do things I’m not...

00:05:37.128 --> 00:05:38.546
Particularly happy about,

00:05:38.546 --> 00:05:42.175
I think, the more lazy weekends I need.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:42.759
The last time

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:44.135
I had to do something in a hurry

00:05:44.135 --> 00:05:45.720
was quite recently.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.555
I think around a month ago

00:05:47.555 --> 00:05:51.726
I moved out of where I was living

00:05:51.726 --> 00:05:53.644
and it was in a different country.

00:05:53.644 --> 00:05:55.271
So what that meant is

00:05:55.271 --> 00:05:56.981
I had to pack my whole life

00:05:56.981 --> 00:05:58.775
into two suitcases,

00:05:58.775 --> 00:06:00.485
since I was moving back home,

00:06:00.485 --> 00:06:01.944
and...

00:06:01.944 --> 00:06:04.238
The reason it was all left to the last minute

00:06:04.238 --> 00:06:05.907
was because I had just went on a trip

00:06:05.907 --> 00:06:07.867
with my boyfriend to Mexico.

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:10.703
So I had around a week

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:12.372
once I came back from that trip

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.040
to pack up everything,

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:14.707
to arrange

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.876
where all my mattresses would go,

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.337
where my couch would go,

00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:21.672
and get rid of everything.

00:06:21.672 --> 00:06:22.632
And

00:06:22.632 --> 00:06:26.219
it was quite an anxiety inducing experience for me,

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:27.303
because

00:06:27.303 --> 00:06:28.513
I'm a very, like,

00:06:28.513 --> 00:06:30.014
organized person,

00:06:30.014 --> 00:06:31.599
even though this doesn't seem like it,

00:06:31.599 --> 00:06:33.518
but I really am.

00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:36.104
And so when I had to

00:06:36.104 --> 00:06:38.314
kind of gather everything,

00:06:38.314 --> 00:06:39.607
it felt very last minute,

00:06:39.607 --> 00:06:41.234
even though I had a week

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.569
and I think till the last hour

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.737
I had to leave,

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.823
like, to go to the airport,

00:06:46.823 --> 00:06:48.449
I was packing things up,

00:06:48.449 --> 00:06:51.452
but thankfully I had a really—

00:06:51.452 --> 00:06:53.287
a really good group of friends

00:06:53.287 --> 00:06:55.748
that were with me blasting music,

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:56.707
helping me pack,

00:06:56.707 --> 00:06:58.084
made it like a really fun,

00:06:58.084 --> 00:07:00.211
enjoyable experience,

00:07:00.211 --> 00:07:02.380
and I think that really helped

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:05.383
also get some momentum to pack.

00:07:05.383 --> 00:07:06.467
Otherwise I was feeling

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:07.760
really lazy about it.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.511
And I think,

00:07:08.511 --> 00:07:09.470
even after I left,

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.305
I left some things behind.

00:07:11.305 --> 00:07:13.891
But my friends went back to my apartment,

00:07:13.891 --> 00:07:16.144
helped me get rid of it, so...

00:07:16.144 --> 00:07:17.603
It was definitely a team effort.

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:18.729
It takes a village.

00:07:18.729 --> 00:07:20.314
We've been discussing an occasion

00:07:20.314 --> 00:07:22.150
when you had to do something in a hurry,

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:24.110
and we're going to talk about

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.154
time management, arriving late,

00:07:26.154 --> 00:07:28.156
managing time, things like that.

00:07:31.826 --> 00:07:33.244
Thought about this question a lot

00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:34.412
because I feel like

00:07:34.412 --> 00:07:36.414
I've been victim to this situation

00:07:36.414 --> 00:07:37.540
a lot of the times.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:39.542
I think it depends

00:07:39.542 --> 00:07:40.877
on how much it happens

00:07:40.877 --> 00:07:42.795
with the same person.

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.505
But I think there's obviously

00:07:44.505 --> 00:07:46.215
some unforeseen circumstances

00:07:46.215 --> 00:07:47.800
that can arise.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.970
I would say that if you can avoid it,

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.264
because time is really limited

00:07:53.264 --> 00:07:55.975
and you want to kind of extend respect

00:07:55.975 --> 00:07:56.934
to your friend.

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:58.019
Show them, you know,

00:07:58.019 --> 00:07:59.645
“I care about your time.”

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:02.523
So it's always best to—

00:08:02.523 --> 00:08:05.109
I personally think, try and arrive on time.

00:08:09.864 --> 00:08:10.448
Again,

00:08:10.448 --> 00:08:12.283
it kind of...

00:08:12.283 --> 00:08:13.075
What I said before,

00:08:13.075 --> 00:08:15.995
bleeds into this answer a little bit, because

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:17.497
I think it’s depending on

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:20.041
how recurring is your situation.

00:08:20.041 --> 00:08:22.043
If there's a certain circumstance

00:08:22.043 --> 00:08:24.003
that happens every morning, maybe,

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:24.795
you know,

00:08:24.795 --> 00:08:25.588
you're a parent

00:08:25.588 --> 00:08:27.507
that has to take care of your child,

00:08:27.507 --> 00:08:30.676
then I think the company should allow

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:31.469
for this

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:32.762
situation to happen

00:08:32.762 --> 00:08:35.389
and not give such extreme consequences.

00:08:35.389 --> 00:08:36.265
I think they should be more

00:08:36.265 --> 00:08:38.768
accepting and understanding.

00:08:38.768 --> 00:08:40.478
But I think if it's just because,

00:08:40.478 --> 00:08:42.522
you know, you've been waking up late

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:44.357
for companies...

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.650
Even though I would,

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:47.485
personally, I would be like “it's okay.”

00:08:47.485 --> 00:08:49.278
I think, you know, time is money,

00:08:49.278 --> 00:08:50.238
especially nowadays,

00:08:50.238 --> 00:08:51.155
in like, this corporate

00:08:51.155 --> 00:08:52.657
capitalistic world.

00:08:52.657 --> 00:08:55.535
So unfortunately, it makes sense

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:57.995
for companies to reprimand.

00:08:57.995 --> 00:09:00.039
But I would say, not too much.

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:02.708
Now let's talk about managing study time.

00:09:09.257 --> 00:09:10.508
I would say shorter chunks.

00:09:10.508 --> 00:09:13.010
I'm also saying this understanding

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:15.137
the era we are in now where

00:09:15.137 --> 00:09:18.057
short form media has also influenced,

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:20.101
like, how we consume information

00:09:20.101 --> 00:09:21.894
and what works best for us.

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:24.105
So I think more than

00:09:24.105 --> 00:09:25.273
“what should people do?”

00:09:25.273 --> 00:09:26.566
It's what I feel

00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:28.442
would be most productive for them.

00:09:28.442 --> 00:09:29.735
And I think that

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:31.612
maybe like, having little breaks in between

00:09:31.612 --> 00:09:33.322
can be like

00:09:33.322 --> 00:09:35.449
kind of motivation.

00:09:35.449 --> 00:09:36.867
“Okay, let me finish this chapter

00:09:36.867 --> 00:09:38.536
and then I'll have like a chocolate.”

00:09:38.536 --> 00:09:40.913
So I think that would be really good.

00:09:45.835 --> 00:09:46.752
I think so.

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:49.088
I recently went to this,

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:52.592
like, virtual VR experience

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:55.011
where I was learning about the Titanic

00:09:55.011 --> 00:09:57.555
by, like, a VR headset and this...

00:09:57.555 --> 00:09:58.723
So I found it

00:09:58.723 --> 00:10:00.474
like a really fun experience.

00:10:00.474 --> 00:10:02.184
It was date night for me,

00:10:02.184 --> 00:10:03.978
but I learned so much.

00:10:03.978 --> 00:10:05.021
And my first thought

00:10:05.021 --> 00:10:07.315
after that experience was

00:10:07.315 --> 00:10:08.858
“I can have fun and learn.”

00:10:08.858 --> 00:10:10.526
And I felt like my mom, being like,

00:10:10.526 --> 00:10:12.111
“You can have fun and learn.”

00:10:12.111 --> 00:10:13.070
But I think that

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.406
they both can go hand-in-hand,

00:10:15.406 --> 00:10:16.449
especially nowadays,

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:17.950
because there's so many

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:19.493
different things available for you

00:10:19.493 --> 00:10:21.078
to really expand

00:10:21.078 --> 00:10:23.414
how you consume information.

00:10:23.414 --> 00:10:24.624
So yeah, I think so.

00:10:24.624 --> 00:10:27.001
Well done. That’s the end of Part three

00:10:27.001 --> 00:10:28.252
and the end of the speaking test.

00:10:28.252 --> 00:10:28.836
Oh, perfect.

00:10:28.836 --> 00:10:30.087
How did you feel about that?

00:10:30.087 --> 00:10:31.589
So nice. I love it.

00:10:31.589 --> 00:10:33.674
Yeah, I think there was no problem for you.

